Oh, JonStar — Episode 137: Differentiation
The World Discovery Crew had encountered a problem.
The Bullamatreans had apparently decided that their name was not going to remain stable.
JonStar stood over the field notes.
Bullametriarchs / Bullamatriarchs
 Bullametrearchs / Bullamatrearchs
He looked at Jonathan.
“Those are four different things.”
Jonathan smiled.
“They are now.”
JonStar frowned.
“That isn't how taxonomy works.”
From somewhere nearby came the sound of an enormous phone being adjusted.
The Bridge Inspector looked up.
“Are any of them bridges?”
“No.”
“Then I have no comment.”
JonStar stared at the four names again.
The problem was becoming more serious.
The variations weren't merely spelling errors anymore. They seemed to carry different sounds, different emphases, and possibly different meanings.
He began carefully marking them in the field notes.
Bullametriarchs
 — original recorded form
Bullamatriarchs
 — divergent form; possibly related
Bullametrearchs
 — pronunciation uncertain
Bullamatrearchs
 — pronunciation even more uncertain
JonStar paused.
Then added:
It is possible that the Bullamatreans themselves distinguish between these forms.
Jonathan leaned over his shoulder.
“Or we're just really bad at spelling.”
JonStar considered this.
“That is possible.”
A beat.
“But much less interesting.”
Jonathan nodded.
“Fair.”
JonStar continued writing.
Then, from the jungle, a Bullamatrean appeared.
It looked at the notes.
It looked at JonStar.
It looked at the four names.
Its expression changed.
JonStar froze.
The Bullamatrean slowly pointed at Bullamatrearchs.
Then at Bullametriarchs.
Then at Bullamatriarchs.
Then at Bullametrearchs.
It shook its head.
JonStar's eyes widened.
“You do distinguish them.”
The Bullamatrean nodded.
Jonathan whispered:
“Oh, this just got worse.”
The creature pointed at JonStar's notebook.
Then very deliberately turned the notebook around.
On the page, beneath the four known variants, it wrote a fifth:
Bullam—
It stopped.
Looked at JonStar.
Stuck out its tongue.
And walked away.
The Bridge Inspector glanced at the page.
“Not a bridge.”
JonStar stared after the creature.
“That's not the important part.”
The Inspector looked at him.
“It is to me.”
Jonathan was laughing.
JonStar closed the notebook.
Field conclusion:
 Further investigation required.
Addendum:
 Do not attempt to pronounce all four forms consecutively.
Secondary addendum:
 Especially after saying “swimsuit.”
Jonathan:
“Why especially then?”
JonStar:
“I don't know.”
From very far away, the Bullamatrean stuck out its tongue again.
End Episode 137.



