Oh, JonStar — Episode 13: The Swimsuit Bridge
JonStar had been quiet for several minutes.
This was generally considered a favorable development.
Jonathan was enjoying Midnight City, experiencing that particular sensation of possibility returning—the feeling that there were things he could still do, places he could still go, worlds still waiting to be discovered.
The Bridge Inspector was inspecting a bridge.
Everything was peaceful.
Then JonStar whispered:
“Swimsuit.”
Jonathan opened one eye.
“No.”
“I was feeling left out.”
The Bridge Inspector stopped moving.
Slowly, he lowered his enormous phone.
“That's not a bridge.”
JonStar smiled.
“I know.”
The Inspector stared at him.
“Then why did you say it?”
“I thought perhaps something interesting might happen.”
Jonathan began laughing.
The Bridge Inspector sighed.
“Pete's sake.”
And then they saw it.
The bridge had changed.
Not dramatically.
Not impossibly.
Just enough.
Across the enormous, perfectly respectable bridge, several sections of the structure now appeared to have acquired the unmistakable visual characteristics of a swimsuit.
There were no boundary lines.
There was no obvious reason.
It was simply—
swimsuit bridge.
JonStar looked delighted.
Jonathan was nearly incapacitated.
The Bridge Inspector walked toward it.
He inspected the first affected section.
Then the second.
Then the third.
He raised his phone.
The phone occupied approximately half his chest.
He took a photograph.
He looked at the result.
He took another.
He looked again.
Finally:
“Structural integrity appears unaffected.”
JonStar brightened.
“So the swimsuit is load-bearing?”
The Inspector looked at him.
“No.”
A pause.
“Probably.”
Jonathan lost it.
The Bridge Inspector returned to his inspection.
JonStar followed.
“Can I cross?”
“You were going to anyway.”
“That is true.”
“Then why ask?”
JonStar considered this.
“Courtesy?”
The Inspector nodded once.
“Good.”
JonStar stepped onto the swimsuit bridge.
Nothing happened.
He walked another ten feet.
Still nothing.
Jonathan watched from the riverbank.
“It's not bleeding anymore.”
JonStar turned.
“Perhaps Planet Welcome has learned boundaries.”
The Bridge Inspector looked up from his phone.
“No.”
Everyone waited.
He pointed at the bridge.
“The bridge learned boundaries.”
Jonathan clapped his hands.
JonStar looked deeply impressed.
The Inspector returned to work.
“Finally. A bridge.”
And somewhere beneath the bridge, the river continued flowing as though none of this were unusual.
Episode 13 ends.

Oh, JonStar — Episode 45: The Bridge Inspector Has a Problem
The Bridge Inspector stopped walking.
This was unusual.
He looked at his enormous phone.
Then at the bridge.
Then at the phone again.
JonStar noticed immediately.
“Problem?”
The Inspector didn't answer.
Jonathan looked up.
“What is it?”
The Inspector held up the phone.
The screen was blank.
Not broken.
Not frozen.
Blank.
JonStar stepped closer.
“Battery?”
“No.”
“Signal?”
“No.”
“Bridge-related?”
The Inspector looked at him.
“No.”
JonStar frowned.
“That sounds serious.”
“It is.”
Jonathan watched the Inspector turn the phone over.
He pressed the side button.
Nothing.
He pressed it again.
Nothing.
For the first time anyone had ever seen, the Bridge Inspector looked genuinely uncertain.
Then he said:
“I can't inspect the bridge.”
JonStar stared.
Jonathan stared.
The bridge continued existing.
This was apparently unacceptable.
JonStar cautiously asked:
“Can you inspect it manually?”
The Inspector looked at him as though he'd suggested inspecting a whale with a teaspoon.
“No.”
“Why?”
“Because the phone tells me what I need to know.”
Jonathan smiled.
“Maybe the universe is trying to tell you something.”
The Inspector looked at Jonathan.
A very long pause.
“Don't.”
Jonathan's smile widened.
JonStar suddenly looked between them.
Something about that exchange felt...
oddly familiar.
The Inspector looked back toward the bridge.
Then toward his dead phone.
Then, unexpectedly, he sighed.
“I may have to cross it.”
JonStar's eyes widened.
“You're going to cross a bridge you haven't inspected?”
The Inspector looked at him.
“Yes.”
Jonathan raised an eyebrow.
JonStar whispered:
“This is unprecedented.”
The Inspector stepped onto the bridge.
Nothing happened.
He took another step.
Still nothing.
He stopped halfway across.
Looked down.
Looked up.
Then quietly said:
“Oh.”
Jonathan waited.
JonStar waited.
The Inspector smiled.
Just slightly.
“I see.”
And suddenly his phone turned back on.
The screen displayed a single message:
BRIDGE: ACCEPTABLE.
JonStar stared.
“That was it?”
The Inspector put the phone away.
“Yes.”
Jonathan looked at him.
“You already knew.”
The Inspector said nothing.
Jonathan frowned.
For just a moment, he had the strange sensation that the Inspector wasn't looking at the bridge.
He was looking at everything.
Then the moment passed.
The Inspector resumed his inspection.
JonStar followed.
Jonathan watched them go.
And somewhere deep beneath the ordinary machinery of the universe, something had just happened that Jonathan was not yet supposed to understand.
End Episode 45.

